#!/usr/bin/python3
# sg-dictate -- voice typing, the native half (Windows' Win+H).
#
# The engine is Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 on the CPU (sgspeech.py). The Windows
# side is sg-shell's sg-dictate.exe, the dictation toolbar: Wine gives it no
# AF_UNIX and no pipes to a native program, so it re-launches itself as
# `sg-dictate --bridge wine <itself> --bridged ...` and this process serves it
# over its standard handles, as sg-netctl's bridge does.
#
#   sg-dictate --transcribe-file WAV...   print what was said (the gate's mode)
#   sg-dictate --listen [--once] [--seconds N]
#                                         dictate from the microphone to stdout
#   sg-dictate --bridge PROGRAM [ARGS]    serve the dictation toolbar
#   sg-dictate --mics [--out FILE]        MIC <name>\t<description>, DEFAULT <name>
#   sg-dictate --meter FILE [--device D] [--seconds N]
#                                         the microphone's level, for "Test
#                                         microphone": LEVEL <0-100> in FILE,
#                                         until N seconds pass or FILE.stop exists
#   sg-dictate --status                   MODEL installed|missing|downloading|failed
#   sg-dictate --download                 fetch the speech model (asks sg-speechd)
#   sg-dictate --remove                   remove it again (administrators)
#   sg-dictate --serve                    sg-speechd: root, one per connection
#
# Privacy: audio is held in memory only while it is recognised, nothing heard
# or typed is logged, and nothing but the explicit model download touches the
# network.
#
